{"parentUuid":"1326efbd-7e0c-4936-9c2e-f83b706520c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsb7TjF5oCu7SLvPSoHj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```ts\nimport { DurableObject } from \"cloudflare:workers\";\n\nconst HOUR_MS = 60 * 60 * 1000;\nconst STATE_KEY = \"state\";\n\nexport interface RoomState {\n  messageCount: number;\n  lastMessage: { author: string; body: string; at: number } | null;\n  lastTickAt: number | null;\n}\n\nconst emptyState = (): RoomState => ({\n  messageCount: 0,\n  lastMessage: null,\n  lastTickAt: null,\n});\n\nexport class ChatRoom extends DurableObject<Env> {\n  // Each operation chains onto this tail, so a read-modify-write never\n  // interleaves with another one across an await.\n  private tail: Promise<unknown> = Promise.resolve();\n\n  private serialize<T>(work: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n    const run = this.tail.then(work);\n    this.tail = run.catch(() => undefined);\n    return run;\n  }\n\n  private async load(): Promise<RoomState> {\n    return (await this.ctx.storage.get<RoomState>(STATE_KEY)) ?? emptyState();\n  }\n\n  private async ensureAlarm(): Promise<void> {\n    if ((await this.ctx.storage.getAlarm()) === null) {\n      await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + HOUR_MS);\n    }\n  }\n\n  async post(author: string, body: string): Promise<RoomState> {\n    return this.serialize(async () => {\n      const state = await this.load();\n      state.messageCount += 1;\n      state.lastMessage = { author, body, at: Date.now() };\n      await this.ctx.storage.put(STATE_KEY, state);\n      await this.ensureAlarm();\n      return state;\n    });\n  }\n\n  async read(): Promise<RoomState> {\n    return this.serialize(() => this.load());\n  }\n\n  async alarm(): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      await this.serialize(async () => {\n        const state = await this.load();\n        state.lastTickAt = Date.now();\n        // Hourly work goes here.\n        await this.ctx.storage.put(STATE_KEY, state);\n      });\n    } finally {\n      await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + HOUR_MS);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe Worker needs a binding and a migration for the class in `wrangler.jsonc`:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"durable_objects\": {\n    \"bindings\": [{ \"name\": \"CHAT_ROOM\", \"class_name\": \"ChatRoom\" }]\n  },\n  \"migrations\": [{ \"tag\": \"v1\", \"new_sqlite_classes\": [\"ChatRoom\"] }]\n}\n```\n\nEach room's alarm reschedules itself indefinitely, so an idle room still runs once an hour. If you want rooms to stop ticking when they go quiet, the alarm handler can skip rescheduling when `messageCount` has not changed since the last tick.\n\nI wrote a per-room `ChatRoom` Durable Object that serializes `post` and `read` through an in-memory promise queue and reschedules its own hourly alarm. I did not run or type-check it, and I did not call the Cloudflare MCP tools because the task only asked for the class."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6425,"cache_read_input_tokens":20945,"output_tokens":4304,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3225},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6425,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4304,"cache_read_input_tokens":20945,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6425},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"d68c2319-4798-4317-a1b2-619ecc8e059c","timestamp":"2026-11-09T15:27:12.834Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionId":"c57fc104-b5a5-40e5-ba8f-67cb9f020802","version":"2.1.319"}
